## Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js App Router project.

### Changes Made

**1. Installed @vercel/analytics package**
   - Added `@vercel/analytics@^2.0.1` to dependencies
   - Used npm to install the package and update lock file

**2. Modified `/app/layout.tsx`**
   - Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
   - Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag (at the end, before closing)
   - Preserved all existing code structure and functionality

**3. Updated dependency files**
   - `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics to dependencies
   - `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and its dependencies

### Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Web Analytics quickstart documentation (retrieved June 23, 2026), I:

1. Fetched the latest installation instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
2. Identified this as a Next.js App Router project (Next.js 16.2.1)
3. Used the framework-specific instructions for Next.js App Router
4. Added the Analytics component to the root layout file as recommended
5. Placed the component at the end of the body tag to ensure it loads after the main content

### Verification

- ✅ Package installed successfully using npm
- ✅ No linting errors introduced
- ✅ Code follows existing patterns and conventions
- ✅ All imports and dependencies properly configured
- ✅ Lock file updated to ensure consistent dependency resolution

### Next Steps for Production

To complete the setup in production:

1. Enable Web Analytics in your Vercel dashboard (Analytics section)
2. Deploy this code to Vercel using `vercel deploy`
3. Verify tracking by checking the browser's Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/*`
4. The Analytics component will automatically track page views and web vitals

### Files Modified

- `app/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component
- `app/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `app/package-lock.json` - Updated lock file with new dependencies

The implementation is complete and ready for deployment!
